 1.187</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.2</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.200</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00, 0.67, 0.20</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.830, 1.153, 0.077</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.9</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">B0-R<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn7-ehp-116-1661">c</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.083</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.822</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02014;</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A1-R</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.088</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00, 0.88, 0.66</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.878</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A2-R</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.082</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.118, 0.813, 0.678</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.3</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A3-R</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.156</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00, 0.64, 0.20</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.724, 1.001, &#x02013;0.281</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.0</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn5-ehp-116-1661"><label>a</label><p>RR model: RR = 1 + &#x003b2; <italic>d</italic> &#x003b8;<italic><sub>f</sub></italic> exp{&#x003c6; <italic><sub>f</sub></italic> ln(<italic>c</italic>)}, where <italic>d</italic> is cumulative arsenic exposure in mg/m3-years, and <italic>c</italic> is airborne arsenic concentration in mg/m<sup>3</sup>. Subscript <italic>f</italic> denotes categories of TSLE or attained age and represents multiple parameters either multiplying the ERR per mg/m<sup>3</sup>-year (&#x003b2;) or distinct categories for the effects of arsenic concentration.</p></fn><fn id="tfn6-ehp-116-1661"><label>b</label><p>Change in deviance from the base model, B0. Difference in deviances provides a likelihood ratio test of the added parameters.</p></fn><fn id="tfn7-ehp-116-1661"><label>c</label><p>Models fit to all cohort data or to restricted data, denoted by &#x0201c;R,&#x0201d; including person-time of workers with time since last exposure &#x0003c; 5 years or age last exposure &#x02265;50. Estimates and 95% CIs: B0 parameters (&#x003b2; and &#x003c6;), 0.115 (0.07&#x02013;0.19) and 1.123 (0.41&#x02013; 1.84); B0-R parameters, 0.083 (0.04&#x02013;0.15) and 0.822 (0.01&#x02013;0.63).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>